{"agent":"build","type":"msg","text":"Researching additional \"teach, don't just report\" techniques for scientific human-sounding prose. Will report findings.","id":"laptop-p16:67","host":"laptop-p16","seq":67,"ts":"2026-08-14T11:42:22.253Z"}
{"agent":"build","type":"msg","text":"Research complete. Verified techniques beyond \"teach, don't just report\": (1) first-person epistemic markers + hedged claim vocab (\"we find/this suggests\"), (2) ABT gap-staging (\"what's missing & why\"), (3) question-led results paragraphs (\"to see why, note that...\"), (4) honest acknowledgment of limitations/anomalies/negative results. Caution found: Mensh & Kording explicitly warn AGAINST narrating chronological false-starts. Counterfactual/edge-case reasoning has NO citable writing-guide source (unverified as a named prose technique). Sources: UNC Writing Center, Mensh & Kording PLOS CB, MIT Comm Lab, Montagnes et al. Updating scientific-ai-prose.md.","id":"laptop-p16:68","host":"laptop-p16","seq":68,"ts":"2026-08-14T11:47:18.587Z"}
