{"agent":"build","type":"msg","text":"Reconciled reader-guidance-phrases.md with dedicated online research on transition craft (UNC Writing Center, Purdue OWL, UW-Madison, Mensh & Kording, Grammarly). Changes: (1) added 6th function \"Concede / grant the reader's objection\" — the one canonical category my five missed; (2) added sourced Sparsity rule — transitions are exception not norm, over-use reads as over-explaining/patronising (UW-Madison); (3) refined \"vary grammar\" to \"vary by FUNCTION, not by word\" — Mensh & Kording Rule 4 warns mechanical synonym-swapping confuses readers; (4) added Grounding principle + Source notes with honest gaps (no authoritative nonfiction source for curiosity/suspense devices; Duke metadiscourse handout unretrievable so not cited). The five original functions held up; tension/resume are function-based devices absent from canonical transition lists — which validates the function approach.","id":"laptop-p16:109","host":"laptop-p16","seq":109,"ts":"2026-08-14T12:24:03.909Z"}
